# File Structure Guidelines

## Directory Organization

The real top-level layout of the frontend — the app this fork actually runs:

```
packages/twenty-front/src/
├── config/             # Runtime/build configuration
├── generated/          # Generated GraphQL types (core)
├── generated-admin/    # Generated GraphQL types (admin)
├── generated-metadata/ # Generated GraphQL types (metadata)
├── hooks/              # App-level hooks
├── loading/            # Loading / bootstrap UI
├── locales/            # Lingui catalogs (*.po) — i18n is Lingui, not JSON
├── localization/       # Locale wiring
├── modules/            # Feature modules — the bulk of the code
├── pages/              # Route-level components
├── testing/            # Test helpers, mocks, decorators
├── types/              # Shared type definitions
└── utils/              # Helper functions
```

There is no `src/components/` and no `src/services/` — shared components live
in `src/modules/ui/` and in the `twenty-ui` package, and data access goes
through the local-db bridge and Apollo, not a services folder.

The research domain of this fork lives inside `modules/`:

```
packages/twenty-front/src/modules/local-db/
├── data-source/        # GraphQL-over-Dexie data source and Apollo providers
├── twenty-local/       # Bridge modes, seeding, workspace reset
└── research/           # Research objects, views, nav, seed data
    ├── manuscript/     # Composer: import, tokens, citations, exports
    ├── import-wizard/  # Upload → map → review → commit → rollback
    ├── components/     # Composer and editor UI
    ├── hooks/
    └── __tests__/
```

The vendored upstream server — **not run by this fork**, and only relevant when
working on the upstream CRM backend:

```
packages/twenty-server/src/
├── command/            # CLI commands
├── constants/
├── database/           # Data source config, instance/workspace commands
├── engine/             # Core engine: metadata, API, auth, twenty-orm
├── filters/            # Exception filters
├── modules/            # Feature modules
├── queue-worker/       # BullMQ worker entrypoint
├── types/
└── utils/
```

There is no `src/entities/` and no `src/dto/` at the server top level — entity
and DTO files live inside the `engine/` and `modules/` feature folders next to
the code that uses them.

## File Naming
- **kebab-case** for all files and directories
- **Descriptive suffixes** for clarity
```
// ✅ Correct naming
user-profile.component.tsx
user-profile.styles.ts
user-profile.test.tsx
user.service.ts
user.entity.ts
create-user.dto.ts
```

## Index Files & Barrel Exports
```typescript
// ✅ Clean barrel exports in index.ts
export { UserCard } from './user-card.component';
export { UserList } from './user-list.component';
export type { UserCardProps, UserListProps } from './types';

// ✅ Usage - clean imports
import { UserCard, UserList } from '@/ui/components/user';
```

## Module Structure
```
src/modules/<feature>/
├── components/     # Module-specific components
├── hooks/          # Module hooks
├── states/         # Jotai atoms and selectors
├── types/          # Type definitions
├── utils/          # Pure helpers
└── __tests__/      # Tests
```

## Import/Export Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Import organization
// 1. External libraries
import { styled } from '@linaria/react';
import { useAtomValue } from 'jotai';

// 2. Internal modules (absolute paths)
import { Button } from 'twenty-ui/input';
import { useAtomStateValue } from '@/ui/utilities/state/jotai/hooks/useAtomStateValue';

// 3. Relative imports
import { UserCardProps } from './types';

// ✅ Named exports only (no default exports)
export const UserComponent = ({ user }: UserProps) => {
  // Component implementation
};
```

Styling is **Linaria** (`@linaria/react`), not styled-components, and state is
**Jotai** (`@/ui/utilities/state/jotai/utils/createAtomState`), not Recoil.

## File Size Guidelines
- **Components**: Under 300 lines
- **Services**: Under 500 lines  
- **Extract logic** into hooks/utilities when files grow large
- **Use composition** over large monolithic components

## Configuration Files

### Project Configuration
```
.vscode/                       # VSCode settings
├── settings.json
├── extensions.json
├── launch.json
└── tasks.json

.github/                       # GitHub workflows and governance
├── workflows/
└── actions/

.cursor/                       # Cursor rules and skills
├── rules/
├── skills/
└── environment.json
```

### Build Configuration
- Keep build configs in root or package directories
- Use consistent naming for config files
- Comment complex configurations
- Version control all configuration files
